  "key_findings": {
    "cyla_v1": "Unbounded neural reranking of the prefix degraded MTF performance significantly (56.7 vs 19.5 steps on alpha=1.6) due to noisy SGD reordering destroying MTF recency guarantees.",
    "cyla_v2": "Restricting the neural scorer to cold items (count == 0) preserved MTF order for hot items, but because cold items all share identical features (zero hits, zero recency) and prefix cold items vanish under repeated queries, CYLA v2 degenerated to exactly replicating MTF search step counts across all regimes while incurring additional neural forward/backward compute overhead."
  }
